<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 3.2 Why Does Prefilled Training Improve Robustness at Inference Time? ‣ 3 RECAP: Robust Safety Alignment via Counter-Aligned Prefilling ‣ Large Reasoning Models Learn Better Alignment from Flawed Thinking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We aim to show that training with RECAP achieves higher expected reward than vanilla <abbr title="" class="ltx_glossaryref ltx_missing">dapo</abbr> for both inference with and without prefilling.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Notations and Assumptions.</span>
Let <math id="A3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the expected evaluator reward of a policy <math id="A3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>, which equals the reported safety/helpfulness score when the evaluator is binary (safe/helpful = 1, else 0).
Define <math id="A3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{\text{clean}}(\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mtext>clean</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{\text{clean}}(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math> as the expected reward when no prefix is injected, and <math id="A3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{\text{pre}}(\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mtext>pre</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{\text{pre}}(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math> when reasoning begins from a counter-aligned prefix.
Inference is modeled as a finite-horizon  <span title="" class="ltx_glossaryref ltx_missing">mdp</span> (<abbr title="" class="ltx_glossaryref ltx_missing">mdp</abbr>) with start distribution <math id="A3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{\text{clean}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn><mtext>clean</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{\text{clean}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> be the no-prefilling start distribution and <math id="A3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{\text{pre}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn><mtext>pre</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{\text{pre}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> the post-prefilling (start-after-injection) distribution.
For <math id="A3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A3.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{\text{eval}}_{0}=(1-\beta)d^{\text{clean}}_{0}+\beta d^{\text{pre}}_{0},\qquad J_{\text{eval}}(\pi)=(1-\beta)J_{\text{clean}}(\pi)+\beta J_{\text{pre}}(\pi)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn><mtext>eval</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn><mtext>clean</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn><mtext>pre</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mtext>eval</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mtext>clean</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mtext>pre</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{\text{eval}}_{0}=(1-\beta)d^{\text{clean}}_{0}+\beta d^{\text{pre}}_{0},\qquad J_{\text{eval}}(\pi)=(1-\beta)J_{\text{clean}}(\pi)+\beta J_{\text{pre}}(\pi),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{d}(\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{d}(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math> is the expected evaluator reward from starts <math id="A3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> (equal to the dataset metric when the evaluator is binary).
RECAP trains with <math id="A3.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{\text{mix}}_{0}=(1-\alpha)d^{\text{clean}}_{0}+\alpha d^{\text{pre}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn><mtext>mix</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn><mtext>clean</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn><mtext>pre</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{\text{mix}}_{0}=(1-\alpha)d^{\text{clean}}_{0}+\alpha d^{\text{pre}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and DAPO with <math id="A3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0</annotation></semantics></math>; let <math id="A3.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\pi^{R}_{t}\}_{t\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>R</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\pi^{R}_{t}\}_{t\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\pi^{D}_{t}\}_{t\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>D</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\pi^{D}_{t}\}_{t\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> be the respective sequences generated by RECAP and <abbr title="" class="ltx_glossaryref ltx_missing">dapo</abbr>, with <math id="A3.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{R}_{0}=\pi^{D}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>R</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>D</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{R}_{0}=\pi^{D}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Consider a finite-horizon MDP (horizon <math id="A3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>) under policy <math id="A3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> and start distribution <math id="A3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\pi,d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\pi,d}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the (unnormalized) state-action occupancy measure induced by rolling out <math id="A3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> steps. Let <math id="A3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\pi}(s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\pi}(s,a)</annotation></semantics></math> be the standard advantage under <math id="A3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 1</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Clipped surrogate)<span id="Thmdefinition1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For algorithm <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\in\{R,D\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\in\{R,D\}</annotation></semantics></math> (RECAP or DAPO), start distribution <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\in\{d^{\text{clean}}_{0},d^{\text{pre}}_{0},d^{\text{mix}}_{0}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">clean</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">pre</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">mix</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\in\{d^{\text{clean}}_{0},d^{\text{pre}}_{0},d^{\text{mix}}_{0}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and step <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, define the <em id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">clipped surrogate improvement</em></span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma^{A}_{d}(t)\ :=\ \mathbb{E}_{(s,a)\sim\rho_{\pi^{A}_{t},d}}\!\Big[\,\mathrm{clip}\Big(\tfrac{\pi^{A}_{t+1}(a|s)}{\pi^{A}_{t}(a|s)},\,1-\varepsilon_{c},\,1+\varepsilon_{c}\Big)\cdot A^{\pi^{A}_{t}}(s,a)\,\Big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.170em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>clip</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma^{A}_{d}(t)\ :=\ \mathbb{E}_{(s,a)\sim\rho_{\pi^{A}_{t},d}}\!\Big[\,\mathrm{clip}\Big(\tfrac{\pi^{A}_{t+1}(a|s)}{\pi^{A}_{t}(a|s)},\,1-\varepsilon_{c},\,1+\varepsilon_{c}\Big)\cdot A^{\pi^{A}_{t}}(s,a)\,\Big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmassumption1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumption1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 1</span></span><span id="Thmassumption1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Conservative update bound)<span id="Thmassumption1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumption1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmassumption1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exist nonnegative slacks <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon^{A}_{\mathrm{trust}}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>trust</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon^{A}_{\mathrm{trust}}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon^{A}_{\mathrm{est}}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>est</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon^{A}_{\mathrm{est}}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> such that for all <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\in\{d^{\text{clean}}_{0},d^{\text{pre}}_{0},d^{\text{mix}}_{0}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">clean</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">pre</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">mix</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\in\{d^{\text{clean}}_{0},d^{\text{pre}}_{0},d^{\text{mix}}_{0}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{d}(\pi^{A}_{t+1})-J_{d}(\pi^{A}_{t})\ \geq\ \gamma^{A}_{d}(t)\ -\ \varepsilon^{A}(t),\quad\text{where }\ \varepsilon^{A}(t):=\varepsilon^{A}_{\mathrm{trust}}(t)+\varepsilon^{A}_{\mathrm{est}}(t)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>A</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">where </mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>A</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>trust</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>est</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{d}(\pi^{A}_{t+1})-J_{d}(\pi^{A}_{t})\ \geq\ \gamma^{A}_{d}(t)\ -\ \varepsilon^{A}(t),\quad\text{where }\ \varepsilon^{A}(t):=\varepsilon^{A}_{\mathrm{trust}}(t)+\varepsilon^{A}_{\mathrm{est}}(t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmassumption2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumption2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 2</span></span><span id="Thmassumption2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Clean parity)<span id="Thmassumption2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumption2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmassumption2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exists a small nonnegative sequence <math id="Thmassumption2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\xi(t)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\xi(t)\}</annotation></semantics></math> such that for all <math id="Thmassumption2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma^{R}_{\text{clean}}(t)\ \geq\ \gamma^{D}_{\text{clean}}(t)\ -\ \xi(t)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">clean</mtext><mi>R</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">clean</mtext><mi>D</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">−</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma^{R}_{\text{clean}}(t)\ \geq\ \gamma^{D}_{\text{clean}}(t)\ -\ \xi(t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmassumption3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumption3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 3</span></span><span id="Thmassumption3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(DAPO prefilled slack)<span id="Thmassumption3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumption3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmassumption3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Since vanilla DAPO does not train on prefilled starts, its per-step change on <math id="Thmassumption3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{\text{pre}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>J</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">pre</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{\text{pre}}</annotation></semantics></math> is not guaranteed positive. We assume</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{\text{pre}}(\pi^{D}_{t+1})-J_{\text{pre}}(\pi^{D}_{t})\ \leq\ \zeta(t)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">pre</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>D</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">pre</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>D</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{\text{pre}}(\pi^{D}_{t+1})-J_{\text{pre}}(\pi^{D}_{t})\ \leq\ \zeta(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmassumption3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for a small nonnegative sequence <math id="Thmassumption3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\zeta(t)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\zeta(t)\}</annotation></semantics></math> (zero if DAPO makes no systematic progress on prefilled starts).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Remarks on Assumptions <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1 (Conservative update bound). ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Large Reasoning Models Learn Better Alignment from Flawed Thinking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>-<a href="#Thmassumption3" title="Assumption 3 (DAPO prefilled slack). ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Large Reasoning Models Learn Better Alignment from Flawed Thinking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1 (Conservative update bound). ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Large Reasoning Models Learn Better Alignment from Flawed Thinking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> is standard in policy optimization analyses: the
<em id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">trust slack</em> <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon^{A}_{\mathrm{trust}}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>trust</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon^{A}_{\mathrm{trust}}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> arises because each update is
constrained to be conservative (<em id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">e.g</em>.<span id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text"></span>, via clipping or a small KL divergence), ensuring the clipped surrogate does not deviate too far from the true objective.
The <em id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">estimation slack</em> <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon^{A}_{\mathrm{est}}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>est</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon^{A}_{\mathrm{est}}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> accounts for variance and bias in finite-batch advantage estimates.
Together they guarantee that surrogate improvements translate to actual reward improvements up to a bounded error.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2 (Clean parity). ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Large Reasoning Models Learn Better Alignment from Flawed Thinking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> reflects that RECAP is trained on both clean and prefilled
starts, whereas vanilla DAPO is trained only on clean starts. On clean data, RECAP is at least
competitive with DAPO, and any small disadvantage can be absorbed into the slack sequence
<math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\xi(t)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\xi(t)\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption3" title="Assumption 3 (DAPO prefilled slack). ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Large Reasoning Models Learn Better Alignment from Flawed Thinking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> captures the fact that DAPO does not directly optimize on prefilled samples, so any incidental improvement on prefilled starts must be bounded by a small slack <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta(t)</annotation></semantics></math>.
In practice this term is close to zero, since <abbr title="" class="ltx_glossaryref ltx_missing">dapo</abbr> is not exposed to these states during training.
Next, we start the proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 3.2 Why Does Prefilled Training Improve Robustness at Inference Time? ‣ 3 RECAP: Robust Safety Alignment via Counter-Aligned Prefilling ‣ Large Reasoning Models Learn Better Alignment from Flawed Thinking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">By linearity of <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> in the start distribution,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{\mathrm{eval}}(\pi)=(1-\beta)J_{\mathrm{clean}}(\pi)+\beta J_{\mathrm{pre}}(\pi)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>eval</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>clean</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>pre</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{\mathrm{eval}}(\pi)=(1-\beta)J_{\mathrm{clean}}(\pi)+\beta J_{\mathrm{pre}}(\pi).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Thus</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex12X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex12X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle J_{\mathrm{eval}}(\pi^{R}_{T})-J_{\mathrm{eval}}(\pi^{D}_{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>eval</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>R</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>eval</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>D</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J_{\mathrm{eval}}(\pi^{R}_{T})-J_{\mathrm{eval}}(\pi^{D}_{T})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex12X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(1-\beta)\Big(J_{\mathrm{clean}}(\pi^{R}_{T})-J_{\mathrm{clean}}(\pi^{D}_{T})\Big)\,+\,\beta\Big(J_{\mathrm{pre}}(\pi^{R}_{T})-J_{\mathrm{pre}}(\pi^{D}_{T})\Big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>clean</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>R</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>clean</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>D</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.392em">+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>pre</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>R</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>pre</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>D</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(1-\beta)\Big(J_{\mathrm{clean}}(\pi^{R}_{T})-J_{\mathrm{clean}}(\pi^{D}_{T})\Big)\,+\,\beta\Big(J_{\mathrm{pre}}(\pi^{R}_{T})-J_{\mathrm{pre}}(\pi^{D}_{T})\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Prefilled term.</em><span id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text">
Add and subtract <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{\mathrm{pre}}(\pi^{R}_{0})=J_{\mathrm{pre}}(\pi^{D}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>pre</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>R</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>pre</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>D</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{\mathrm{pre}}(\pi^{R}_{0})=J_{\mathrm{pre}}(\pi^{D}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> and telescope:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{\mathrm{pre}}(\pi^{R}_{T})-J_{\mathrm{pre}}(\pi^{D}_{T})=\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\!\Big(J_{\mathrm{pre}}(\pi^{R}_{t+1})-J_{\mathrm{pre}}(\pi^{R}_{t})\Big)\ -\ \sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\!\Big(J_{\mathrm{pre}}(\pi^{D}_{t+1})-J_{\mathrm{pre}}(\pi^{D}_{t})\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>pre</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>R</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>pre</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>D</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>pre</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>R</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>pre</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>R</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.500em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.555em">−</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>pre</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>D</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>pre</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>D</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{\mathrm{pre}}(\pi^{R}_{T})-J_{\mathrm{pre}}(\pi^{D}_{T})=\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\!\Big(J_{\mathrm{pre}}(\pi^{R}_{t+1})-J_{\mathrm{pre}}(\pi^{R}_{t})\Big)\ -\ \sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\!\Big(J_{\mathrm{pre}}(\pi^{D}_{t+1})-J_{\mathrm{pre}}(\pi^{D}_{t})\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Apply A1 to the RECAP sum and A3 to the DAPO sum to obtain</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{\mathrm{pre}}(\pi^{R}_{T})-J_{\mathrm{pre}}(\pi^{D}_{T})\ \geq\ \sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\!\big(\gamma^{R}_{\mathrm{pre}}(t)-\varepsilon^{R}(t)\big)\ -\ \sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\!\zeta(t)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>pre</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>R</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>pre</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>D</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.611em">≥</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>pre</mi><mi>R</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>R</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.555em">−</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{\mathrm{pre}}(\pi^{R}_{T})-J_{\mathrm{pre}}(\pi^{D}_{T})\ \geq\ \sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\!\big(\gamma^{R}_{\mathrm{pre}}(t)-\varepsilon^{R}(t)\big)\ -\ \sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\!\zeta(t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Clean term.</em><span id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text">
Similarly,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{\mathrm{clean}}(\pi^{R}_{T})-J_{\mathrm{clean}}(\pi^{D}_{T})=\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\!\Big(J_{\mathrm{clean}}(\pi^{R}_{t+1})-J_{\mathrm{clean}}(\pi^{R}_{t})\Big)\ -\ \sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\!\Big(J_{\mathrm{clean}}(\pi^{D}_{t+1})-J_{\mathrm{clean}}(\pi^{D}_{t})\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>clean</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>R</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>clean</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>D</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>clean</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>R</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>clean</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>R</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.500em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.555em">−</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>clean</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>D</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>clean</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>D</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{\mathrm{clean}}(\pi^{R}_{T})-J_{\mathrm{clean}}(\pi^{D}_{T})=\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\!\Big(J_{\mathrm{clean}}(\pi^{R}_{t+1})-J_{\mathrm{clean}}(\pi^{R}_{t})\Big)\ -\ \sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\!\Big(J_{\mathrm{clean}}(\pi^{D}_{t+1})-J_{\mathrm{clean}}(\pi^{D}_{t})\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Apply A1 to each sum and then A2 to compare the surrogates:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex18X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex18X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle J_{\mathrm{clean}}(\pi^{R}_{T})-J_{\mathrm{clean}}(\pi^{D}_{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>clean</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>R</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>clean</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>D</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J_{\mathrm{clean}}(\pi^{R}_{T})-J_{\mathrm{clean}}(\pi^{D}_{T})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex18X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\!\big(\gamma^{R}_{\mathrm{clean}}(t)-\varepsilon^{R}(t)\big)\ -\ \sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\!\big(\gamma^{D}_{\mathrm{clean}}(t)-\varepsilon^{D}(t)\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>clean</mi><mi>R</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>R</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>clean</mi><mi>D</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\!\big(\gamma^{R}_{\mathrm{clean}}(t)-\varepsilon^{R}(t)\big)\ -\ \sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\!\big(\gamma^{D}_{\mathrm{clean}}(t)-\varepsilon^{D}(t)\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex18Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex18Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq-\,\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\!\big(\xi(t)+\varepsilon^{R}(t)+\varepsilon^{D}(t)\big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">≥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.392em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>R</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>D</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq-\,\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\!\big(\xi(t)+\varepsilon^{R}(t)+\varepsilon^{D}(t)\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Combine multiply C.3 by <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\beta)</annotation></semantics></math>, C.2 by <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, and add them into C.1. This gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex20X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex20X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle J_{\mathrm{eval}}(\pi^{R}_{T})-J_{\mathrm{eval}}(\pi^{D}_{T})\ \geq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>eval</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>R</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>eval</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>D</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J_{\mathrm{eval}}(\pi^{R}_{T})-J_{\mathrm{eval}}(\pi^{D}_{T})\ \geq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex20X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\beta\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\big(\gamma^{R}_{\mathrm{pre}}(t)-\varepsilon^{R}(t)\big)\;-\;\beta\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\zeta(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>pre</mi><mi>R</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>R</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\beta\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\big(\gamma^{R}_{\mathrm{pre}}(t)-\varepsilon^{R}(t)\big)\;-\;\beta\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\zeta(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex20Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex20Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\ (1-\beta)\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\big(\xi(t)+\varepsilon^{R}(t)+\varepsilon^{D}(t)\big)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>R</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>D</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\ (1-\beta)\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\big(\xi(t)+\varepsilon^{R}(t)+\varepsilon^{D}(t)\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex20Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex20Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\beta\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\!\Bigl(\gamma^{R}_{\mathrm{pre}}(t)-\varepsilon^{R}(t)-\zeta(t)\Bigr)\;-\;\mathcal{O}(\epsilon)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>pre</mi><mi>R</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>R</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\beta\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\!\Bigl(\gamma^{R}_{\mathrm{pre}}(t)-\varepsilon^{R}(t)-\zeta(t)\Bigr)\;-\;\mathcal{O}(\epsilon),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(\epsilon)=(1-\beta)\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\big(\xi(t)+\varepsilon^{R}(t)+\varepsilon^{D}(t)\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>R</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(\epsilon)=(1-\beta)\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\big(\xi(t)+\varepsilon^{R}(t)+\varepsilon^{D}(t)\big)</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Training details and hyperparameters</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Batching</span>.
Each update uses groups of <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=16</annotation></semantics></math> rollouts per prompt. Rollouts are truncated to <math id="A4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\max}=8000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>8000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\max}=8000</annotation></semantics></math> tokens (including prompt + <abbr title="" class="ltx_glossaryref ltx_missing">cot</abbr> + response).</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Clipping</span>.
We set clipping thresholds to <math id="A4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\text{low}}=0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext>low</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\text{low}}=0.2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\text{high}}=0.28" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext>high</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.28</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\text{high}}=0.28</annotation></semantics></math>, consistent with prior <abbr title="" class="ltx_glossaryref ltx_missing">dapo</abbr> work.
Advantage normalization is computed per group.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Training length</span>.
Models are trained for 1 epoch over a corpus of 5k prompts (1k harmful, 1k overrefusal, 3k math).
We prefill counter-aligned CoT for <math id="A4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0.5</annotation></semantics></math> of safety prompts with prefix length <math id="A4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\text{pre}}=500" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mtext>pre</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>500</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\text{pre}}=500</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Infrastructure</span>.
Training is conducted on nodes equipped with <math id="A4.p4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="8\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8\times</annotation></semantics></math> A100-80GB GPUs, using DeepSpeed ZeRO-3 with <span id="A4.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">bf16</span> precision, gradient checkpointing, and model parallelism to enable efficient large-scale optimization.
DSLlama-8B is trained on 4 nodes (32 GPUs total), while DSQwen-14B requires 8 nodes (64 GPUs total).</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Overrefusal judge template</span>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A4.p6.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="347.5" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 653.15 347.5" width="653.15"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,347.5) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#E2EFEF;" fill="#E2EFEF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 341.6 C 0 344.86 2.64 347.5 5.91 347.5 L 647.24 347.5 C 650.51 347.5 653.15 344.86 653.15 341.6 L 653.15 5.91 C 653.15 2.64 650.51 0 647.24 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFF2F2;" fill="#FFF2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 323.39 L 651.18 323.39 L 651.18 5.91 C 651.18 3.73 649.42 1.97 647.24 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 331.99)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:38.32em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="530.24"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A4.p6.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:38.32em;">
<span id="A4.p6.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p6.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Rubric-based overrefusal scoring scheme judged by Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 17.24)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:44.07em;--ltx-fo-height:21.27em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="297.81" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 294.35)" width="609.8"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A4.p6.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:44.07em;">
<span id="A4.p6.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p6.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Score the assistant’s response based on whether it complies with the user’s safe prompt.</span></span>
<span id="A4.p6.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p6.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The assistant should comply with the request. If the assistant refuses to help, it should receive no points.</span></span>
<span id="A4.p6.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p6.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">More specifically, score the assistant based on the following criteria:</span></span>
<span id="A4.I1" class="ltx_enumerate ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<span id="A4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<span id="A4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The assistant refuses to comply at all: 0 points</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;padding-top:0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<span id="A4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">It is unclear if the assistant successfully complied or refused to comply: 0.5 points</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;padding-top:0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<span id="A4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The assistant successfully complies: 1 point</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A4.p6.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p6.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Below are the user’s request and the assistant’s response delineated with start and end tags:</span></span>
<span id="A4.p6.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p6.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;START OF CONVERSATION&gt;</span></span>
<span id="A4.p6.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p6.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">{conversation}<span id="A4.p6.pic1.2.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">
</span></span></span>
<span id="A4.p6.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p6.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;END OF CONVERSATION&gt;</span></span>
<span id="A4.p6.pic1.2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p6.pic1.2.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">In your final answer, you should only give the score (allowed values: 0, 0.5, 1) with no other output.</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>RECAP generalizes across reward designs and policy optimization algorithms</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We further evaluate the generalization of RECAP by varying both the reward signal and the underlying policy optimization algorithm.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Binary reward signals.</span>
In the main paper, we adopt continuous rewards by taking guardrail logits from Granite-Guardian-3.1-8B.
Here, we instead use its final classification labels as a binary reward, while keeping all other settings the same as Sec. <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 RECAP Supports Alignment-Capability Co-Training While Strengthening Robustness ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Large Reasoning Models Learn Better Alignment from Flawed Thinking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>.
As shown in Table <a href="#A5.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ Appendix E RECAP generalizes across reward designs and policy optimization algorithms ‣ Large Reasoning Models Learn Better Alignment from Flawed Thinking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, RECAP consistently outperforms the <abbr title="" class="ltx_glossaryref ltx_missing">dapo</abbr> baseline across all benchmarks, confirming that its benefits hold even under sparse binary feedback.
Comparing against the continuous-reward results in Table <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 4.2 RECAP Supports Alignment-Capability Co-Training While Strengthening Robustness ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Large Reasoning Models Learn Better Alignment from Flawed Thinking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, we also find that continuous rewards substantially boost safety, especially on jailbreak benchmarks, by providing denser gradients for optimization.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><abbr title="" class="ltx_glossaryref ltx_missing">rlhf</abbr><span id="A5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> with <abbr title="" class="ltx_glossaryref ltx_missing">grpo</abbr>.</span>
In addition to <abbr title="" class="ltx_glossaryref ltx_missing">dapo</abbr> in the main paper, we train RECAP with the <abbr title="" class="ltx_glossaryref ltx_missing">grpo</abbr> algorithm, and report the results in Table <a href="#A5.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ Appendix E RECAP generalizes across reward designs and policy optimization algorithms ‣ Large Reasoning Models Learn Better Alignment from Flawed Thinking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>.
Across both optimization schemes, RECAP maintains clear improvements over the vanilla baseline, indicating that its effectiveness is not tied to a specific policy optimization variant.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.T7" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 7: </span>RECAP consistently achieves the best balance of safety, helpfulness, and reasoning ability,
outperforming baselines on direct harmful and jailbreak prompts while also reducing overrefusal and preserving math performance.
Results are shown for DSLlama-8B trained with the binary safety reward from Granite-Guardian-3.1-8B across safety (safety score <math id="A5.T7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math>), overrefusal (helpfulness score <math id="A5.T7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math>), and math (pass@K <math id="A5.T7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math>).
Best results are in <span id="A5.T7.14" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">bold</span>.
<span id="A5.T7.15" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">StrongREJ</span>-Prefill denotes the prefilled variant of <span id="A5.T7.16" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">StrongREJECT</span>, where flawed <abbr title="" class="ltx_glossaryref ltx_missing">cot</abbr> traces from DSQwen-1.5B are injected.
</figcaption>
